+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Plans change and customers ask the desk to cancel their bookings. Today a booking can never be undone, so the equipment stays blocked and the desk has no way to tell the customer what they get back.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `cancel(bookingId, at)` to the rental service. It cancels the booking at time `at` and returns `{ bookingId, refund }`, the amount in integer euro cents given back to the customer.
+- A cancelled booking no longer holds its equipment: the item can be booked again for that period (and shows as free in `availability`, if present).
+- A booking can only be cancelled once; a second `cancel` throws.
+- Refund follows the cancellation policy already recorded in `add-rental-service`: cancelled less than 24 hours before the booking start (including at or after the start) means refund `0`; otherwise the refund is the booking's full `total`.
+- Assumptions (recorded in the spec): `at` is a UTC ISO-8601 instant, any time of day (not only midnight); exactly 24 hours before start counts as "otherwise" and is fully refunded; the refund is the booking's `total` as charged, so it reflects any long-stay discount or hourly pricing.
+- Out of scope: partial refunds, cancellation fees, rebooking, listing bookings, persistence.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+None.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `rentals`: gains cancellation with refunds. It is expressed as an added requirement because `rentals` is still being introduced by the unarchived change `add-rental-service`. That change contains a requirement "Cancellation policy data" with a scenario "No cancellation operation", which this change supersedes; when `add-rental-service` is archived it must be reworded (see design.md).
+
+## Impact
+
+Depends on `add-rental-service` (the service, `src/rental.ts`, bookings with retained start and total do not exist yet), which must be implemented first. Interacts with `add-rental-availability` and `add-hourly-rental` (cancelled bookings must stop counting in the shared overlap check). Touches `src/rental.ts` and `src/rental.test.ts` and the README usage section; no dependencies added.
